IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-43. NOUNS of a cross-reference. No rule is written here; the facts below are what a reader of the two texts could state.
-- TARGET COMPILER: main. No REFUSE, no section GIVEN, no TYPICALLY, no YMD, no sets: a case the sources do not answer is NOTHING from a MAYBE.
--
-- This row is NOT an encoding of the Foreign Workers Law, 5751-1991. It records citations: for each, what the citing words say they point at, what the target is,
-- and where each of the two readings comes from. A citation whose two descriptions differ is a defect, and is kept in an expected-red file.
--
-- THE KINDS BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's: each is a short plain description I wrote from reading the citing words and the target, so that two descriptions of the same
-- thing are the same kind. The Law's own words are quoted beside each value in the references module (`src:` lines are the Foreign Workers Law consolidation, `ext:[nii]` lines
-- are the National Insurance Law consolidation, `ext:[SH ...]` lines are typed from a page image of the official instrument and checked against its text layer).

§ `Nouns of a cross-reference`

DECLARE `What a provision is about` IS ONE OF
    `the definition of the retirement age`
    `the definition of the nursing benefit`
    `the definition of a suspended permit`
    `a definition that was deleted, so that the section prints no text for the term`
    `a person with a medical disability fixed under items 33, 34 or 91, or found to need constant supervision`

DECLARE `Where a reading comes from` IS ONE OF
    `the official instrument, read from its page image`
    `the consolidation only`

DECLARE `A cross-reference` HAS
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `the citing words say it points at` IS A `What a provision is about`
    `the target is` IS A `What a provision is about`
    `the target was deleted from the official text on` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `limb (a) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
    `limb (b) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
